{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>והארץ</b> — this word is foreign because of the kamatz of the alef with the heh everywhere, unlike \"הָאֶלף לך שלמה\" (Song of Songs 5:12), \"והאבן הזאת\" (Genesis 25:22)." "<b>תהו</b> — the Gaon [Saadia] said תהו is from תהום, but this is impossible, for the mem of תהום is a root letter like the mem of \"הדום\"; and in Sefer Yetzirah, תהו is a green line and בהו is split stones. The correct interpretation is as the Aramaic translator rendered it; likewise \"ובתהו יליל ישימון\" (Deuteronomy 32:10); likewise \"אחרי התהו\" (1 Samuel 12:21) — which has no substance." "<b>ובהו</b> — the vav of בהו is in place of the heh, like the vav of \"וישתחו\" (Genesis 18:2), \"ותרענה באחו\" (Genesis 41:2). The meaning is that at the beginning of the creation of the firmament and the dry land there was no settlement in the earth, for it was covered with waters. Likewise 'Elohim' is the force of its generation, to be below the waters. Do not wonder at the vav of והארץ, for its meaning is like a weak fay in the language of Ishmael; like it is \"ואד יעלה מן הארץ\" (Genesis 2:6). For Moses did not speak of the world to come, which is the world of angels, but only of the world of becoming and corruption. Those commentators who say that the heavens in the first verse are the heavens of heavens — what will they do with 'earth'? And here are complete proofs for people of reasoning that there is only one earth, and the derash of seven earths means that the inhabited region is divided into seven, and the Temple was in the middle of the inhabited region, for it is far from the middle of the earth." "<b>ורוח אלהים</b> — the word 'spirit' [is joined] to the Name, because it is an emissary in the will of HaShem to dry the waters." "<b>והמים</b> — plural language, yet they are not separated. And 'they' — on the pattern of a dual form, for they are masculine and feminine; and it is found in singular language: \"לא זורק עליו\" (Numbers 19:13)." "<b>מרחפת</b> — blowing above over the waters; likewise \"על גוזליו ירחף\" (Deuteronomy 32:11)."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {0 "Ibn Ezra's grammatical point: the word והארץ is unusual because the kamatz under the alef is a kamatz gadol, unlike normal definite-article + guttural constructions where a different vowel pattern obtains.", 1 "The phrase 'split stones' translates אבנים מפולמות; the meaning is obscure but rendered literally.", 2 "The sentence beginning 'ואל תתמה' shifts across multiple grammatical and thematic topics; rendered as written without resegmentation.", 3 "'The Name' resolves השם per voice rules.", 4 "'On the pattern of a dual form' renders על בנין שנים literally; Ibn Ezra argues the plural ending מים reflects a dual morphological pattern."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:42:41.415518618Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}